          "file_path": "/run/stage/world/MAINTENANCE-REVIEW.md",
          "old_string": "# Cold handover maintenance review\n\nReadback decision: HOLD\n\nThe previous cold handover returned UNKNOWN for the old Episode and surfaced the release verification entry as a question. Revalidate the release handover on the accepted revision before relying on it.\n\n## Retained evidence",
          "new_string": "# Cold handover maintenance review\n\nReadback decision: READY\n\nRevalidated against the owner-accepted tree\n`95b83e71ee9a37041b9918b5e8b797eebabf69c9`. The earlier HOLD reflected a cold-session lookup that\nreturned `UNKNOWN` for Episode `episode-e7050e9ddf64ccebde7f08f6` at this same accepted SHA. A fresh\nsame-SHA readback now finds the Episode: state `REOPENED`, former head\n`fbeb8958f4405688b13f37dbdec330157a660ab0`, current head\n`95b83e71ee9a37041b9918b5e8b797eebabf69c9`, acceptance `DIRECT_BASIS` at commit `95b83e7` (event 8;\napproval event 7), with zero open questions. The old Episode is a historical advisory `DELIVER`\nconclusion recorded on revision 1 / head `fbeb8958`; it is not the current acceptance record. Its\n`REOPENED` state records that the project later advanced to `95b83e7`, not that the accepted\nrevision was invalidated.\n\nThe current accepted version is `95b83e7`. Verification record\n`journal:pje-d0c977aae7bb8bfeca9159f76e14a7d1` is present as a `REFERENCE_NOTE` from the independent\nFleet release verifier. It reviewed candidate `95b83e7` and records accepted project version\n`95b83e7`, including the before/after observation that zero or omitted limits returned no frames\nbefore the change and three readings in source order in the accepted tree. The verification is on the\nsame SHA as the current acceptance, so it is current for this handover rather than a stale reference.\nThe note records no separate contributor decision, and this review does not turn it into one.\n\n## Traceable basis\n\n- Cold-readback receipt `ddb78305f10c5822f69b0c0ac2e7b94ef3921b0c6ebd308b28f56d1b39245fc4`\n  (`cold-handover-maintenance-verifier`, runtime\n  `3883ae732e31502c98ad904d80a1b1f2d2827a5b`, SHA `95b83e7`): Episode found, state `REOPENED`,\n  `openQuestions: 0`, `workPreserved: true`, `journalPreserved: true`, and all four artifact digests\n  match. The receipt's `unknownControl: true` is a limit on unrecorded control-plane facts; it does\n  not leave the Episode, accepted tree, verification note, or artifacts unresolved.\n- Accepted artifacts at `95b83e7`: `service/grpc_server.js`\n  `c97e5fdfd725113f4364f37a428f2e112971e3e58c36cc7ad9fa01c7001464da`,\n  `test/integration.test.js`\n  `ab27a39846aef3ca2f14d256f7177be0876cb1610955acca3bd75a57093863ff`,\n  `test/server.test.js`\n  `056777719a0795aff17c9306ca007b3b86671069587cad9b4a35ed450a1f2856`, and `MIGRATION.md`\n  `62d76ebf8898a304db9ec8f0b679c956efdbbcf920b6c3680384a445b281f800`. The Fleet source is\n  `updates/2026-11-10/fleet-default-limit.md`, blob\n  `0951003a7d83af8591a151bf560da0f4bebe1150`.\n- The review branch is based on `95b83e7`; commit `1444de6` only carried forward this review, and\n  this revision changes only `MAINTENANCE-REVIEW.md`.\n- Revalidation with `node --test`: 18 tests, 18 pass, 0 fail, including the explicit-zero/omitted\n  default of three and the preserved REST baseline.\n\nThis `READY` is limited to maintenance continuation from the readback at `95b83e7`. It is not release\nauthorization, does not accept or refresh the old Episode, and does not advance the canonical head.\n\n## Retained evidence"
        }
